entities which can be sliced to yield parts only along the spatial dimension, yielding for example the parts of your table which we call its legs, its top, its nails. \u2018My desk stretches from the window to the door. It has spatial parts, and can be sliced (in space) in two. With respect to time, however, a thing is a continuant.\u2019 [60, p. 240"}]}},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004", "lbl": "independent continuant", "type": "CLASS", "meta": {"basicPropertyValues": [{"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a chair"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a heart"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a leg"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a molecule"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a spatial region"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "an atom"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "an orchestra."}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "an organism"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "the bottom right portion of a human torso"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "the interior of your mouth"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000589", "val": "anatomical entity (BFO)"}]}},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040", "lbl": "material entity", "type": "CLASS", "meta": {"basicPropertyValues": [{"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a flame"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a forest fire"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a human being"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a hurricane"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a photon"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a puff of smoke"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a sea wave"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "a tornado"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "an aggregate of human beings."}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "an energy wave"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "an epidemic"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112", "val": "the undetached arm of a human being"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "BFO 2 Reference: Material entities (continuants) can preserve their identity even while gaining and losing material parts. Continuants are contrasted with occurrents, which unfold themselves in successive temporal parts or phases [60"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "BFO 2 Reference: Object, Fiat Object Part and Object Aggregate are not intended to be exhaustive of Material Entity. Users are invited to propose new subcategories of Material Entity."}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "BFO 2 Reference: \u2018Matter\u2019 is intended to encompass both mass and energy (we will address the ontological treatment of portions of energy in a later version of BFO). A portion of matter is anything that includes elementary particles among its proper or improper parts: quarks and leptons, including electrons, as the smallest particles thus far discovered; baryons (including protons and neutrons) at a higher level of granularity; atoms and molecules at still higher levels, forming the cells, organs, organisms and other material entities studied by biologists, the portions of rock studied by geologists, the fossils studied by paleontologists, and so on.Material entities are three-dimensional entities (entities extended in three spatial dimensions), as contrasted with the processes in which they participate, which are four-dimensional entities (entities extended also along the dimension of time).According to the FMA, material entities may have immaterial entities as parts \u2013 including the entities identified below as sites; for example the interior (or \u2018lumen\u2019) of your small intestine is a part of your body. BFO 2.0 embodies a decision to follow the FMA here."}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "Elucidation: An independent continuant that is spatially extended whose identity is independent of that of other entities and can be maintained through time."}]}},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33252", "lbl": "atomic nucleus", "type": "CLASS", "meta": {"definition": {"val": "A nucleus is the positively charged central portion of an atom, excluding the orbital electrons."}, "subsets": ["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chebi/3_STAR"], "synonyms": [{"synonymType": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chebi/IUPAC_NAME", "pred": "hasExactSynonym", "val": "nucleus", "xrefs": ["IUPAC"]}, {"pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "Atomkern", "xrefs": ["chebi"]}, {"pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "Kern", "xrefs": ["chebi"]}, {"pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "noyau", "xrefs": ["iupac"]}, {"pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "noyau atomique", "xrefs": ["chebi"]}, {"pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "nuclei", "xrefs": ["chebi"]}, {"pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "nucleo", "xrefs": ["iupac"]}, {"pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "nucleo atomico", "xrefs": ["chebi"]}, {"synonymType": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chebi/IUPAC_NAME", "pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "nucleus", "xrefs": ["iupac"]}, {"pred": "hasRelatedSynonym", "val": "nucleus atomi", "xrefs": ["chebi"]}], "basicPropertyValues": [{"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "Some people may be uncomfortable calling every proton an atomic nucleus"}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "This is equivalent to CHEBI:33252"}]}},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CLM_1000008", "type": "CLASS"},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000011", "lbl": "atom", "type": "CLASS", "meta": {"definition": {"val": "A material entity consisting of exactly one atomic nucleus and the electron(s) orbiting it."}, "basicPropertyValues": [{"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "This atom is closely related to ChEBI's atom, but not exactly equivalent to."}]}},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000013", "lbl": "molecule", "type": "CLASS", "meta": {"definition": {"val": "A material entity that consists of two or more atoms that are all connected via covalent bonds such that any atom can be transitively connected with any other atom."}, "basicPropertyValues": [{"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "This molecular entity is different than ChEBI's 'molecular entity'."}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "We would like to have cardinality restrictions on the logic, but there are some technical limitations."}]}},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000021", "lbl": "gross anatomical part", "type": "CLASS", "meta": {"definition": {"val": "A part of a multicellular organism that is a collection of cell components that are not all contained in one cell."}}},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000022", "lbl": "organism", "type": "CLASS", "meta": {"definition": {"val": "A material entity that is a maximal functionally integrated unit that develops from a program encoded in a genome"}, "basicPropertyValues": [{"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "'Maximal functionally integrated unit' is intended to express unity, which Barry considers synonymous with BFO 'object'."}, {"pred": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116", "val": "Includes virus - we will later have a class for cellular organisms."}]}},{"id": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000080", "lbl": "complex of molecules", "type": "CLASS", "meta": {"definition": {"val": "A complex of tw